IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 2: ss 3 to 5 -- the exclusive privilege, its exceptions and the power to license.
-- (ss 6 to 10, 12 to 14: deferred, see COVERAGE.md.  s 11: sgta-s11-approval.l4.)
--
-- FORK 2 (recorded in TV-QUESTION.md section 4; NOTES.md points there): s 3(2)(a) lists "using" among the rights of the privilege, while the offence in
-- s 53(1) lists only "establishes, installs, maintains, provides or operates" and then adds "or otherwise
-- infringes the privilege conferred upon the Authority by section 3".  Whether the closing words carry the
-- additional verbs of s 3(2)(a) into the offence is a reading.  This module records both verb lists separately and
-- sgta-part6-offences.l4 takes the closing words as written (the offence covers any act that infringes the privilege).

§ `s 3 Exclusive privilege`

-- src:565 | 3.—(1) As from 1 December 1999 and subject to this Act, the
-- src:566 | Authority has the exclusive privilege for the operation and provision
-- src:567 | of telecommunication systems and services in Singapore.
@ref s 3(1) (src:565-567)
GIVEN `act` IS AN `Act on a telecommunication system or service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1): the act is one of the operation or provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `act`
    WHEN `operating` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `providing` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:571 | (a) includes the rights of establishing, installing, using,
-- src:572 | working, maintaining, developing, constructing,
-- src:573 | promoting, hiring and selling telecommunication systems
-- src:574 | and services; and
@ref s 3(2)(a) (src:571-574)
GIVEN `act` IS AN `Act on a telecommunication system or service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(2)(a): the act is one of the rights the privilege includes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `act`
    WHEN `establishing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `installing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `using` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `working` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `maintaining` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `developing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `constructing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `promoting` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hiring` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:565 | 3.—(1) As from 1 December 1999 and subject to this Act, the
-- src:566 | Authority has the exclusive privilege for the operation and provision
-- src:567 | of telecommunication systems and services in Singapore.
-- src:569 | (2) The privilege conferred on the Authority by subsection (1) —
-- src:571 | (a) includes the rights of establishing, installing, using,
-- src:572 | working, maintaining, developing, constructing,
-- src:573 | promoting, hiring and selling telecommunication systems
-- src:574 | and services; and
-- src:576 | (b) extends to every vessel or aircraft registered in Singapore
-- src:577 | and every other vessel, aircraft and any vehicle, whether
-- src:578 | mechanically propelled or not, in Singapore.
@ref s 3 (src:565-578)
GIVEN `act` IS AN `Act on a telecommunication system or service`
      `in Singapore, or on a vessel, aircraft or vehicle to which s 3(2)(b) extends the privilege` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3: the act is within the Authority's exclusive privilege` MEANS
        `in Singapore, or on a vessel, aircraft or vehicle to which s 3(2)(b) extends the privilege`
    AND (   `s 3(1): the act is one of the operation or provision` `act`
         OR `s 3(2)(a): the act is one of the rights the privilege includes` `act`)

§ `s 4 Exceptions to section 3`

-- src:582 | 4. The privilege conferred by section 3 is not infringed by —
-- src:584 | (a) the running by a person solely for the person’s own use or
-- src:585 | solely for the purposes of the person’s business (but not for
-- src:586 | providing any telecommunication service to another
-- src:587 | person) of a telecommunication line system in which all
-- src:588 | the equipment comprised therein is situated —
-- src:590 | (i) on a single set of premises in single occupation; or
-- src:592 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:593 | 13 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:595 | (ii) in a vessel, aircraft or vehicle or in 2 or more vessels,
-- src:596 | aircraft or vehicles mechanically coupled together;
-- src:597 | or
-- src:599 | (b) the operation of any telecommunication system in the
-- src:600 | course of their duties by the officers and men and women
-- src:601 | of the Singapore Armed Forces, the Singapore Police
-- src:602 | Force, the Singapore Civil Defence Force or of any visiting
-- src:603 | force lawfully present in Singapore.
@ref s 4(a) and (b) (src:582-603)
GIVEN `is a telecommunication line system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is run solely for the person's own use or solely for the purposes of the person's business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is used to provide a telecommunication service to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all its equipment is on a single set of premises in single occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all its equipment is in one vessel, aircraft or vehicle, or in 2 or more mechanically coupled together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is operated in the course of their duties by SAF, Police, SCDF or a visiting force lawfully present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4: the privilege is not infringed` MEANS
        (    `is a telecommunication line system`
         AND `is run solely for the person's own use or solely for the purposes of the person's business`
         AND (NOT `is used to provide a telecommunication service to another person`)
         AND (   `all its equipment is on a single set of premises in single occupation`
              OR `all its equipment is in one vessel, aircraft or vehicle, or in 2 or more mechanically coupled together`))
    OR `is operated in the course of their duties by SAF, Police, SCDF or a visiting force lawfully present`

§ `s 5 Power to license telecommunication systems and services`

-- src:607 | 5.—(1) A licence may, with the consent of, or in accordance with
-- src:608 | the terms of a general authority given by the Minister, be granted by
-- src:609 | the Authority either unconditionally or subject to such conditions as
-- src:610 | the Authority may impose and specify in the licence and either
-- src:611 | irrevocably or subject to revocation as therein specified for the
-- src:612 | running of such telecommunication systems and services falling
-- src:613 | within section 3 as are specified in the licence.
-- src:615 | (2) A licence granted under subsection (1) may be granted either to
-- src:616 | any person, class of persons or a particular person, and may include
-- src:617 | (without affecting the power to impose conditions conferred by that
-- src:618 | subsection) conditions requiring —
@ref s 5(1) and (2) (src:607-618)
-- (s 5(7), quoted in the Act but not encoded as a test: no person is to question whether the Minister's consent
-- was given, so the grant is taken as made once the Authority has granted it; consent is therefore not an input.)
GIVEN `the Authority has granted a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system or service falls within s 3 and is specified in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(1): this licence authorises the running of the system or service` MEANS
        `the Authority has granted a licence`
    AND `the system or service falls within s 3 and is specified in the licence`

-- src:705 | (8) The grant of licences under this section is at the discretion of the
-- src:706 | Authority.
@ref s 5(8) (src:705-706)
GIVEN `the Authority decides to grant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(8): a licence is granted` MEANS
    `the Authority decides to grant`

-- src:713 | (10) Anything done under and in accordance with a licence granted
-- src:714 | under subsection (1) does not constitute an infringement of the
-- src:715 | privilege conferred by section 3.
@ref s 5(10) (src:713-715)
GIVEN `done under and in accordance with a licence granted under s 5(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(10): the act is not an infringement of the privilege` MEANS
    `done under and in accordance with a licence granted under s 5(1)`
